## Steps

### 1. Cloud inventory (rclone — read-only, runs while transfers continue)

Run these commands sequentially (size checks can be slow on large remotes):

```powershell
# Top-level structure of each remote
rclone lsd "gdrive-personal:" 2>&1
rclone lsd "dropbox:" 2>&1
rclone lsd "onedrive:" 2>&1

# Sizes (may take a few minutes each — run with --fast-list for speed)
rclone size "dropbox:" --fast-list 2>&1
rclone size "onedrive:" --fast-list 2>&1

# INGEST progress snapshot
rclone lsd "gdrive-personal:INGEST/windows-2026-05-12" 2>&1
rclone size "gdrive-personal:INGEST/windows-2026-05-12" --fast-list 2>&1
```

### 2. Local Windows inventory (PowerShell)

```powershell
# Top-level dirs under C:\Users\loganf with sizes (skip system/rebuild dirs)
Get-ChildItem "C:\Users\loganf" -Directory | 
  Where-Object { $_.Name -notin @('node_modules','scoop','openclaw_env','.sbx-denybin','.ollama') } |
  ForEach-Object {
    $size = (Get-ChildItem $_.FullName -Recurse -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Measure-Object -Property Length -Sum).Sum
    [PSCustomObject]@{ Folder = $_.Name; SizeGB = [math]::Round($size/1GB, 2) }
  } | Sort-Object SizeGB -Descending | Format-Table -AutoSize

# Work OneDrive top-level
Get-ChildItem "C:\Users\loganf\OneDrive - Idaho Public Television" -Directory |
  Select-Object Name | Sort-Object Name
```

